    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense is positioned for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, whose 74.55 score leads the team. Facing Brandon Young (4.77 xERA), **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a massive 14% boost due to his dynamic platoon advantage, making him our anchor against a vulnerable arm. **Josh Lowe** also draws a premium matchup against Roki Sasaki; despite the 5.23 xERA suggesting a potential blowout, **Josh Lowe** sees a substantial 19% boost from the starter\u2019s profile, securing his place as a primary producer. While **Jackson Merrill** faces the toughest matchup of our starters against George Kirby (3.45 xERA), his elite sprint speed keeps him in the lineup despite the SP skill penalty, as we prioritize stolen base potential to mitigate the efficiency dip.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Coby Mayo**, who finished with a 56.01 score\u2014narrowly missing the cut. While **Coby Mayo** offered a solid profile against Lovelady, he was ultimately displaced by the overall higher projected efficiency of **Andy Pages** and **Dominic Smith**, both of whom benefit from more favorable lineup positioning or higher park factors. Managers should keep a close eye on **Gunnar Henderson**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Josh Lowe**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Andy Pages**, and **Nolan Schanuel**, as their statuses remain \"Lineup Pending.\" Should any of these bats be relegated to the bottom of the order, their daily efficiency scores will be subject to immediate downward revision. \n\nFinally, while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (66.82) remains a locked-in core piece, we are monitoring the wind conditions impacting **Sam Antonacci** and **Miguel Vargas** on the bench; their scores were suppressed by unfavorable weather, contributing to their exclusion. **Drake Baldwin** (67.37) is the surprise standout of the lower order, earning a significant boost from an favorable matchup against Bello and a prime #1 spot in the lineup, making him a sneaky candidate for runs scored today. As we hunt for category gains, the Waves are optimized to exploit the weaker arms in the rotation while navigating the volatile weather and lineup risks inherent to this slate.",
